<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 230 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 230 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 230 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GM0 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.2 BLN    1.0 BLN    1.0 BLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    600 MLN#   700 MLN    930 MLN    =</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  T-BILLS	100 MLN*   100 MLN*   230 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   200 MLN*   =	    =	    =</p>
<p># INCLUDES 300 MLN BILLS/FRG REPO TO OCT 28 AT 5-23/32 PERCENT</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
